   * The status of a task follows a linear lifecycle: open (work not yet started, default) → in-progress (actively being worked on) → completed (work finished) → closed (fully resolved). Each status transition is strictly sequential — tasks cannot skip statuses or move backwards through the flow. On successful status change, an immutable audit entry is recorded in the task history tracking the previous status, new status, timestamp, and the employee who performed the transition.
   *
   * Only users with task management authority can change task status. This includes the task's assigned employee, project-leads within the project, and users with organization-level project:view permission. Unauthorized status change attempts are rejected.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param projectId UUID of the project that owns the task. Provides project context for authorization and task lookup.
   * @param taskId UUID of the task whose status will be updated. Must belong to the specified project.
   * @param body The new status value to apply to the task. Must follow the linear progression: open → in-progress → completed → closed.
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor member
   * @x-autobe-specification Validate the task exists and belongs to the specified project (hrm_time_tracking_project_id matches projectId). Check the requesting employee has authority to change status: must be the task's assigned employee, a project-lead on this project, or have project:manage permission. Validate the status transition follows the linear flow: open → in-progress → completed → closed. Reject backwards transitions (e.g., completed → in-progress) with a 422 error. Reject transitions that skip statuses (e.g., open → completed) with a 422 error. Assign updated_at to current timestamp. In a transaction: (1) update the task's status field, (2) create a new hrm_time_tracking_task_histories record with previous_status (the old status before update), new_status (the requested status), hrm_time_tracking_task_id, hrm_time_tracking_employee_id (the current employee), and created_at = now. Return the full updated task record.
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post()
